From: Zephyr 4.4 / SDK 1.0.1 port
Subject: [PATCH] libmicroros: force-include strings.h for gcc >= 14

gcc >= 14 (Zephyr SDK 1.0.1 ships 14.3.0) makes
-Wimplicit-function-declaration a hard error in C. rcutils'
src/strcasecmp.c calls strcasecmp/strncasecmp without including
<strings.h> (neither does its own rcutils/strcasecmp.h declare them) —
it only ever worked by implicit declaration, which gcc <= 13 (SDK
0.17.x) downgraded to a warning.

picolibc declares both functions unconditionally in <strings.h>
(no feature-test guard), so force-include the header into every colcon
C TU to give the whole micro-ROS stack the correct prototypes.
Masking with -Wno-error=implicit-function-declaration would leave the
same latent implicit-decl UB in place; C++ flags are untouched (C++ has
never allowed implicit declarations, so no C++ TU relies on them).

Signed-off-by: Hermes (for Chris Gammell)

diff --git a/modules/libmicroros/libmicroros.mk b/modules/libmicroros/libmicroros.mk
--- a/modules/libmicroros/libmicroros.mk
+++ b/modules/libmicroros/libmicroros.mk
@@ -10,6 +10,13 @@
 CFLAGS_INTERNAL := $(X_CFLAGS)
 CXXFLAGS_INTERNAL := $(X_CXXFLAGS)
 
+# gcc >= 14 (SDK 1.0.1) makes implicit-function-declaration a hard error.
+# rcutils/src/strcasecmp.c calls strcasecmp/strncasecmp without including
+# <strings.h> (implicit decls were only a warning on gcc <= 13 / SDK 0.17.x).
+# picolibc declares both unconditionally in <strings.h>; force-include it so
+# every C TU gets the prototypes instead of masking with -Wno-error.
+CFLAGS_INTERNAL := -include strings.h $(CFLAGS_INTERNAL)
+
 # picolibc: rcutils enables Annex K mid-translation-unit (#define
 # __STDC_WANT_LIB_EXT1__ 1 in error_handling.h), but picolibc only typedefs
 # __errno_t/__rsize_t in sys/_types.h when the macro is already set at FIRST